+## Change log — 0.9.7_Hardened_4
+
+**Hardened_4 closes ODR-020.** It defines how the existing N1 diagnostic applies when
+a namespace prefix resolves and the final member does not. This changes diagnostic
+selection, presentation, span and fix-it only. No Ember source program changes validity;
+no module/import, visibility, overload, type, ownership, lifetime, ABI or runtime behavior
+changes.
+
+Every normative edit below is **DIAGNOSTIC / TOOLING HARDENING**. It does not add a
+diagnostic code or a second suggestion/ranking system.
+
+| # | Change | Class | Where |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| H4.1 | **Qualified paths are a specialization of N1.** Resolve the namespace prefix first; enumerate only member names legally visible through that namespace under `[MOD-2]` and the existing resolver; compare spelling against the unresolved final identifier only; keep the existing N1 rank and top-three limit; display the original source-qualified prefix and candidate; highlight and replace only the final identifier. A failed prefix gets the ordinary prefix-resolution diagnostic and never triggers a final-member search. | DIAGNOSTIC / TOOLING HARDENING | XX.6.2, N1 |
+| H4.2 | **Conformance and regression evidence.** Add qualified-alias and nested-path suggestions, token-local source spans and edits, alias preservation, public and same-package candidates, private and cross-package `pub(package)` exclusion, ranked top-three candidates, deterministic output, failed-prefix handling, no-candidate handling, and the unchanged direct-`from` import behavior. | DIAGNOSTIC / TOOLING HARDENING | `tests/conformance/DIA-12/`, `compiler/ember_driver/tests/ui.rs` |
+| H4.3 | **No language or diagnostic identity change.** The existing `E1010` unknown-name family remains in use in this revision; no `E1060` or other code is introduced. This change adds no accepted program, import behavior, visibility rule, ranking key, runtime operation, or ABI surface. | DIAGNOSTIC / TOOLING HARDENING | XX.6.2 |
+
+**ODR-019 dependency.** This H4 is authored from `0.9.7_Hardened_3`, which does not
+incorporate ODR-019's cross-file tie policy. H4 therefore does not redefine or duplicate
+cross-file ranking. A source revision that already carries ODR-019 MUST continue applying
+its same-file/cross-file ordering to the qualified candidate set.
+
+The complete owner ruling is preserved byte-for-byte at
+`docs/spec-source/as-received/ODR-020_qualified_path_N1.md`. H4 is a frozen development
+target, not a change to the repository's adopted `0.8.5_Hardened_1` source.
+
+**Implementation checklist.**
+
+- [x] Keep invalid qualified names rejected and leave successful path resolution unchanged.
+- [x] Resolve namespace prefixes before final-member candidate discovery.
+- [x] Use the existing namespace/member and visibility facts; exclude inaccessible names.
+- [x] Compare only the unresolved final segment and preserve the source alias/prefix in help.
+- [x] Attach the diagnostic primary span and machine-applicable edit to the final token only.
+- [x] Reuse N1 ranking, threshold, deterministic ordering and top-three cap; add no ranking key.
+- [x] Keep `from` imports, module/import semantics, language validity, ABI and runtime unchanged.
+- [x] Cover the specified behavior with DIA-12 conformance and UI regressions.
+
+**This change log is exhaustive for the H4 normative delta.**
