+
+For N1 on a qualified path of the form `<prefix>::<name>`, the compiler MUST
+resolve `<prefix>` first using the existing module/namespace resolver. If that
+prefix does not resolve, the ordinary path-resolution diagnostic MUST identify
+the unresolved prefix component; the compiler MUST NOT search for suggestions
+for `<name>`. Only after the prefix resolves may the compiler enumerate the
+items eligible for lookup through that namespace under `[MOD-2]` and the
+existing import/visibility rules. Private or otherwise inaccessible items MUST
+NOT enter this candidate set; `pub(package)` items are eligible only where the
+existing package-visibility rule permits access. Candidate discovery MUST reuse
+the resolver's namespace/member facts, not a diagnostic-only symbol table or a
+scan of unrelated modules.
+
+The spelling-distance comparison MUST use only the unresolved final identifier
+`<name>` and the candidate's final identifier. It MUST use the existing N1
+distance threshold, ranking and maximum suggestion count; qualified names add
+no ranking key or separate algorithm. For each candidate, help MUST render the
+original source-spelled prefix followed by `::` and the candidate's final name.
+This preserves aliases exactly: `io::pritn` suggests `io::print`, not a
+canonical declaration path. For nested paths, preserve every source prefix
+component in the same way.
+
+The primary unresolved-name span and the machine-applicable replacement MUST
+cover only the unresolved final identifier token. For `io::pritn`, the help
+renders `io::print`, while the edit replaces only `pritn` with `print`; it MUST
+NOT rewrite `io::pritn` as one whole-path edit. The diagnostic remains in the
+existing unknown-name family and MUST NOT introduce a diagnostic code or alter
+which programs are accepted. A direct `from a.b import x` binding continues to
+use ordinary, unqualified N1.
 
